dary_2", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "<span class=\"strong\"> Accepting and Refusing Invitations </span>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you invite someone, you use the modals <span class=\"italic\">would</span>, <span class=\"italic\">should</span> and <span class=\"italic\">could</span>. <br/> For example: <br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Would you like to come to dinner?</span> <br/>  <span class=\"italic\">You should come to my party!</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">Could you come over later?</span><br/>You can also use the phrase <span class=\"italic\"> How about ... ?</span>  <br/><br/> It is important to respond in a polite way when a person invites you.<br/> You thank a person when you accept an invitation.<br/> You apologize when you refuse an invitation."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Andrew:</span> How about eating pizza tonight? My treat!<br/><span class=\"strong\">Bobby:</span> Thanks! That's very kind of you!"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Accepting an Invitation</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Refusing an Invitation</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class = \\\"italic\\\">With pleasure!<br/>Thank you so much!<br/>That's very kind/sweet of you.<br/>Thank you for ...<br/>Great idea!</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class = \\\"italic\\\">Thanks, but ... </span><br/><span class = \\\"italic\\\">I would love to, but ... </span><br/><span class = \\\"italic\\\">I'm really sorry, but ... </span><br/><span class = \\\"italic\\\">Thank you for the offer, but ... </span><br/><span class = \\\"italic\\\">Sorry about that!</span><br/><span class = \\\"italic\\\">Maybe next time!</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Jenna:</span> Would you like to watch an action movie?<br/><span class=\"strong\">Roy:</span> I would love to, but I need to work tonight."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Jessica:</span> You should come over for dinner later! <br/> <span class=\"strong\">Marie:</span> Great idea!"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to veg out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to spend free time doing nothing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I love to veg out in front of the TV!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le01ob10aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when you make plans with your friends."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "messy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not clean; not neat"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Chinese food is great but it's messy to eat in front of the TV."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le01ob10aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "I hope you don't mind"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "I hope you are OK with it."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: John and Sally are coming. I hope you don't mind!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le01ob10aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "besides"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in addition; as well"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Let's invite John. I know you are good friends."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le01ob10aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to keep someone company"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to spend time with someone when they feel bored or lonely"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I like all my friends to keep me company!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le01ob10aud05"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn3le01ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Think of something to do tonight. Write a dialogue."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Invite your partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Respond to the invitation. Do you accept or refuse?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Accept? Use the right expressions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Refuse? Use the right expressions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Exchange roles."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I accept and refuse invitations."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write 30 to 50 words about plans for the evening."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use 3 target words about making plans."}]}], "type": "sena"}